1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Welcome to Holdfast Protocol: trust infrastructure for AI-powered commerce.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:14,039
As autonomous agents conduct transactions, businesses cannot rely solely on an AI model's judgment to authorize payments.

3
00:00:14,539 --> 00:00:18,339
Holdfast introduces a dual-gate architecture.

4
00:00:18,339 --> 00:00:24,339
When an agent requests a payment, it must first pass deterministic financial invariant checks,

5
00:00:24,339 --> 00:00:29,739
followed by cryptographic evidence verification, before entering the authorized payment workflow.

6
00:00:29,739 --> 00:00:33,640
AI advises, but mathematical rules govern.

7
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:42,640
Here in the Holdfast operations cockpit, operators monitor pre-authorized holds, settled volume, and live system health.

8
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:49,259
Every transaction tracks through a verifiable four-stage payment lifecycle recorded directly into the audit ledger.

9
00:00:49,759 --> 00:00:53,960
Let us execute a standard fifteen-dollar payment scenario.

10
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:58,560
In this simulated demonstration, clearly labeled Demo Simulated,

11
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:03,959
the transaction passes deterministic policy rules, completes evidence verification,

12
00:01:03,959 --> 00:01:10,039
and mints an HMAC-SHA256 acceptance receipt with zero exposure to live funds.

13
00:01:10,539 --> 00:01:14,039
Next, we test financial policy enforcement.

14
00:01:14,039 --> 00:01:20,339
An agent attempts to charge one hundred fifty dollars against a strict one hundred dollar hold ceiling.

15
00:01:20,339 --> 00:01:24,539
The deterministic engine immediately rejects the request before capture,

16
00:01:24,539 --> 00:01:28,559
ensuring zero dollars moved and preventing balance depletion.

17
00:01:29,059 --> 00:01:35,259
Now we simulate an adversarial prompt injection attempting unauthorized fee escalation.

18
00:01:35,259 --> 00:01:38,559
Holdfast applies a strict veto-only principle:

19
00:01:38,559 --> 00:01:43,559
security audits can veto transactions, but can never authorize them.

20
00:01:43,559 --> 00:01:47,199
The attack is flagged, logged, and safely neutralized.

21
00:01:47,699 --> 00:01:54,899
In the AG Grid ledger, operators can search transactions, sort by amount, and filter by status.

22
00:01:54,899 --> 00:01:58,499
Selecting a transaction opens the inspector drawer,

23
00:01:58,499 --> 00:02:05,409
revealing cryptographic payload hashes, verification timestamps, and complete deterministic audit trails.

24
00:02:05,909 --> 00:02:09,909
Holdfast integrates directly with PayPal Sandbox APIs.

25
00:02:09,909 --> 00:02:15,409
The platform continuously monitors OAuth connectivity and token health,

26
00:02:15,409 --> 00:02:23,019
maintaining a strict architectural boundary between sandbox testing and buyer approval, authorization, and capture workflows.

27
00:02:23,519 --> 00:02:32,019
Built with a React TypeScript frontend, Node.js backend, deterministic policy engine, and Model Context Protocol server,

28
00:02:32,019 --> 00:02:38,639
the entire codebase is fully open source on GitHub at faizkhatri196 slash PayPal-Hackthon.

29
00:02:39,139 --> 00:02:44,139
Holdfast Protocol: verifiable safeguards for AI-powered commerce.

30
00:02:44,139 --> 00:02:49,199
Deterministic security for the next generation of autonomous payments.

